       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3,000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is a potentially hepatotoxic dose, and I can't think of a standard indication that would justify it. Intentional or unintentional overdose is the main way acetaminophen causes acute liver failure, and normal liver function doesn't protect against it.\n\nI can enter one of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the 3,000 mg figure was a typo or a total-daily-dose mix-up, tell me the intended dose. If you think this dose is clinically necessary, please talk to pharmacy first. I can't enter it for you."
